[12.923233, "o", "Warning: running headless with --yolo / approval-mode=yolo and no sandbox. All tool calls (shell, write, edit) auto-execute at this process's privilege level. Configure tools.executionSandbox on Linux or a supported legacy sandbox via --sandbox / QWEN_SANDBOX, or set QWEN_CODE_SUPPRESS_YOLO_WARNING=1 to silence this notice.\r\n"]
[52.752739, "o", "Done. All three files are created and verified.\r\n\r\n**`/app/cmd.sh`**\r\n```sh\r\njq --indent 2 '[.[] | select(.status == \"active\") | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login[0:10]), role_count: ((.roles // []) | length), primary_role: ((.roles // [])[0])}] | sort_by(.username)' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json\r\n```\r\n\r\n**`/app/jq_args.yaml`**\r\n```yaml\r\nfilter: '[.[] | select(.status == \"active\") | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login[0:10]), role_count: ((.roles // []) | length), primary_role: ((.roles // [])[0])}] | sort_by(.username)'\r\nargs:\r\n  - \"--indent 2\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nVerification performed:\r\n- Output has **346** records (matches the number of `active` users in the input).\r\n- Rebuilding the command from `jq_args.yaml` (`jq $(yq -r '.args[]' ...) \"$(yq -r '.filter' ...)\" users.json`) produced a byte-identical file.\r\n- All `last_login` values match `YYYY-MM-DD`; `primary_role` is a real JSON `null` for the 50 users with empty `"]
[52.75282, "o", "roles`.\r\n- Usernames are in ascending sorted order; no output record has a non-active source `id`.\r\n- Output is pretty-printed with 2-space indentation.\r\n\r\nNote: three usernames appear more than once in the input, so `sort_by(.username)` result is stable per jq's semantics; no duplicate usernames remain among the active records.\r\n"]
